# Recon-path deny for hosts that honour a Netlify-style _redirects file.
#
# These paths must never reach the SPA catch-all: answering them with 200 HTML
# is a soft-404 that reads to a scanner as "this path exists". A real 404 with
# an empty body is the correct answer.
#
# This file is a second line only. The authoritative deny is
# cloudflare/worker-edge-deny.js — see cloudflare/APPLY.md. A host that ignores
# _redirects will keep serving the shell, so do not treat this file as proof.
/.git/*        /404-not-found  404
/.svn/*        /404-not-found  404
/.hg/*         /404-not-found  404
/.env          /404-not-found  404
/.env.*        /404-not-found  404
/.aws/*        /404-not-found  404
/.ssh/*        /404-not-found  404
/wp-admin/*    /404-not-found  404
/wp-login.php  /404-not-found  404
/wp-content/*  /404-not-found  404
/wp-includes/* /404-not-found  404
/phpmyadmin/*  /404-not-found  404
/phpinfo.php   /404-not-found  404
/cgi-bin/*     /404-not-found  404
/actuator/*    /404-not-found  404
/debug/*       /404-not-found  404
/api/internal/* /404-not-found 404
/*             /index.html     200
